{
  "requirement": "During one call to `verify`, direct reads by the criterion and\nreads served by the SDK's agent tools record inputs in the same\n`ValidationContext`. For example, if criterion code reads a test and the agent\nthen reads its helper, both node fingerprints accompany the returned answer.\nA subsequent verification starts with an empty dependency list.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Obligations derived.** The requirement text implies four structural obligations:\n1. Direct criterion reads and agent-tool reads write into one `ValidationContext`.\n2. Reads served by the agent tools land in that same context.\n3. Both kinds of read keep their node fingerprints.\n4. Each verification starts with an empty trace.\n\n**Mapping to source.**\n- **One shared trace.** `crates/trust-but-verify/src/procedure.rs#struct[ValidationContext]` holds a single `observations` mutex-guarded `Vec<Dependency>`.\n  - Direct reads go through `ValidationContext::read` and `read_snapshot`. `read_snapshot` calls `prepare_read` and then `record_read`, which appends to `observations`. Successors take the parallel route through `outgoing_edges` and `observe_edges`.\n  - `dependencies()` returns that same trace.\n- **Agent receives the same context.**\n  - `procedure.rs#impl[Ask<'a, 'd, D, R, P>]#2/fn[execute]` passes `self.ctx` itself to `agent.run(request, self.ctx)`.\n  - The `Agent::run` implementation in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/tools.rs#impl[ToolAgent<P, T>/Agent<D>]/fn[run]` takes `inspection: &ValidationContext` and stores it in a `GraphSession`. The struct `GraphSession` holds only a shared reference (`inspection: &'a ValidationContext`) and keeps no trace of its own.\n- **Agent-tool reads are recorded in that context.**\n  - `GraphSession::dispatch` handles `read_node` and `outgoing_edges` with `prepare_read` and `prepare_edges`. It queues the resulting `Dependency::Node` or `Dependency::OutgoingEdges` entries, with their fingerprints, in `pending`. Source-tool deliveries are added to `pending` too.\n  - `GraphSession::delivered` drains `pending` into the shared context through `record_read` and `observe_edges`.\n  - `agent.rs#fn[converse]` calls `session.delivered()` after each provider response. Direct reads and agent reads therefore end up in the same list, and both fingerprints accompany the answer. `graph.rs#fn[execute_with_context]` returns `ctx.dependencies()` as the answer's dependencies.\n- **Empty start for each verification.**\n  - `graph.rs#fn[verify]` builds a fresh `ValidationContext::new(...)` for every call.\n  - `ValidationContext::configured` initializes `observations: Default::default()`.\n  - No state carries over between calls.\n\n**Observations, not gaps.** The fresh-context behavior comes from `verify`, `new` and `configured`. None of them carries a `shared_context` reference. They are reached from `verify`, which is not marked `impl` for this requirement. They also only construct the type, and the marked items, which hold the shared trace, are what meet the requirement. I did not treat this as a gap. The obligations are fulfilled by the type structure and the marked roots.\n\nI found no structural gaps and no applicable `{fixme}`. Tests exist, for example `agent/tests.rs#fn[concurrent_tool_agents_isolate_histories_pages_and_submissions_and_share_reads]`. This was a structural assessment, so I did not assess test adequacy.",
  "references": "2c35862fa48dbc05e8825f322f614b0f35937ab779b0239d61752080a67691e4",
